+A role on Claude Code is outside all of this.
+Its conversation is Claude Code's own transcript, under the role's `CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR` on the issue's volume, never a row of Oh My Pi's table, so its generation is told neither session variable and its launcher stats that file as a `pvc` launch does;
+a replacement pod continues it with `--resume <session id>`, the id read from the recorded path.
+Two consequences hold whatever `session_store` says:
+`legion sessions import` refuses such a transcript, naming it (that one-off copy fills Oh My Pi's table, which holds no session of a transcript), and neither it nor `legion sessions mark-lost` counts the transcript `missing` from that table, so mark-lost leaves its claim as it is;
+and a Claude claim with a session to resume expects the issue's volume (`LEGION_EXPECT_ISSUE_VOLUME`), so a lost volume is `workspace-init`'s loud refusal rather than a quiet fresh agent.
+The recreated-workspace notice reaches it too: its own MCP server (`packages/claude-envoy`) reads `LEGION_WORKSPACE_RECREATED` at start and writes the same text into the session over the bridge's inbox, once per launch, recorded beside the phase reminder's state so a restarted server does not repeat it.
